Formal separation of supervision and control&nbsp;


The SL AA introduces an unusual structure whereby PG personnel will perform common work solely under the direction of LD, but remain
 employed and supervised by PG. Indeed, we understand that the Board intends for PG personnel to carry out generic/firm-specific work under PG’s direction. This formalises a split between line management and professional control that is not addressed, let alone
 authorised, in the Pan-NOx AA. That agreement permits delegation of work to another firm, not delegation of the
supervision of one firm’s employees to another while the employer retains all employment obligations.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


b.
Governance over PG’s internal personnel decisions&nbsp;


