The SL AA changes the status quo in material ways such that it cannot be said that what is being proposed is
 “exactly what we have all been working under” or that “this will not practically change much day to day.”&nbsp;&nbsp;


&nbsp;


2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
Tension with Employment Contracts&nbsp;

Because the SL AA goes beyond what is authorised in the Pan-NOx AA, it creates direct tension with the terms of PG employment contracts.
 You advise that “there will be no change to your employment contract” and that “consent by employees is not necessary for PG to execute the agency agreement.” We respectfully disagree.&nbsp;


