Hi Carolina &nbsp;Please see the statement attached. &nbsp;In case helpful you can find all the funding disclosure applications and accompanying docs in this folder: &nbsp;[For Counsel] Funding Disclosure Applications&nbsp;Let me know if there’s anything else I can do to help. &nbsp;Best Jess &nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 06 November 2025 12:44To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;@Jessica Fechner Could you let me know where I can find the witness statement that is defined as Boddy 11, pls? The questions addressed to me refer to that document. &nbsp;Regarding tax, I believe the implications can be materially significant, as the basic premise of our financial model and our financial statements is that the facilities are true loans. &nbsp;I am not an accountant or tax lawyer, but claiming that the funding is a fee-sharing arrangement would automatically exclude it from being a loan as a business-to-business structure. We should speak to David Kan and Donatas. I think they’ve discussed this with auditors and big 4 firms, so I would not take the risk without further investigation. &nbsp;We should consider whether characterizing this as a fee-sharing arrangement would automatically exclude it from being treated as a loan under a business-to-business structure. My concern is that this might create room for potential inconsistencies with our previous statements. &nbsp;I will call Matt and try to bring DK in as we spoke on Teams.&nbsp;Kind regards &nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 06 November 2025 04:17To: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;Carolina&nbsp;I've raised the two points with Pallas - I dont think PACCAR is an issue and Gramercy have confirmed they are fine to concede the point.&nbsp;&nbsp;Im not sure on what basis being a funder re-classifies the credit agreement as anything other than a loan but I am not a tax specialist so defo could be wrong - this is not something Pallas can speak to either I suspect and we may need to take the risk.&nbsp;Please can I have the information I requested about Fulcrum/Locke asap this morning so that we can start to finalise - please can this be prioritised.&nbsp;Thanks​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Wednesday, November 5, 2025 10:50 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Disclosure application - AA2 WS &nbsp;Thanks, Anna. I will review the doc in more detail, but the main question that Pallas can help with, if they haven’t considered this yet, is whether taking the position of a “funder” under CPR 25.28(b) could impact the treatment of the credit agreement and its characterisation as a fee-sharing arrangement, as considered in PACCAR. If there is an overlap between these concepts, it may be difficult for Gramercy to accept CPR 25.28(b), depending on the risk that the credit agreement could be deemed unenforceable. I am not familiar with the details of the case law, but it may be worth looking/discussing it with Boies if Pallas hasn’t done so yet. There are a few clauses in the credit agreement pasted below where PG represented that the Credit Agreement is not a fee sharing agreement for the PACCAR purpose.&nbsp;Another important aspect of this is tax consequences. If assuming the position of a “funder” under CPR 25.28(b) would result in the credit agreement being reclassified as something other than a loan or debt, this could adversely affect the deductibility of interest for corporation tax purposes. &nbsp;&nbsp;6.30. 58AA Courts and Legal Services Act 1990. Each Borrower shall not, andshall cause each of the Credit Parties and their respective Affiliates not to, directly or indirectly, (a)challenge the enforceability of this Agreement, any Credit Document, the G1 Facility CreditAgreement, any other G1 Facility Funding Documentation, the G2 Facility Credit Agreement or anyother G2 Facility Funding Documentation for any reason whatsoever, including by reference tos.58AA Courts and Legal Services Act or any analogous law, regulation or theory, including but notlimited to by reference to R (PACCAR) v Competition Appeal Tribunal [2023] UKSC 28 or (b) takethe position that this Agreement (or any portion hereof) is not governed exclusively by, or notconstrued, determined and enforced exclusively in accordance with, the laws of the State of NewYork (without regard to conflict of laws principles thereof exclusively by New York).&nbsp;8.24. Relationship Between Secured Parties and Borrowers. Each Credit Partywaives any right to bring any private cause of action or any suit of any nature against any Lender or the Lender Representative (or any of their respective officers, directors, employees, agents orrepresentatives) in connection with any alleged violation of any applicable Disciplinary Rules. EachCredit Party waives any right to assert any defense to the payment of the Obligations based on aviolation of any applicable Disciplinary Rules. Each Credit Party acknowledges that it has enteredinto this Agreement and all Credit Documents with the Secured Parties, each of which is a nonlawyer.The Borrowers and the Secured Parties hereby agree that this Agreement and the otherCredit Documents evidence a loan and financing agreement wherein the Lenders are providingfinancing to the Borrowers, and the Borrowers represent to the Secured Parties that the contemplatedtransactions do not constitute in any manner a fee sharing agreement between any of the SecuredParties and the Borrowers, and it is the intent of the Borrowers to strictly comply with the applicableDisciplinary Rules. The Borrowers and the Secured Parties acknowledge and agree that no SecuredParty has a contingent or other interest in the outcome of any Case. The Secured Parties shall haveno direct contact with the Clients, and the Secured Parties shall have no influence or control overthe litigation strategy with respect to any Case. The Secured Parties shall not interfere, and theBorrowers shall not allow any interference by any Secured Party, with the attorney-clientrelationship in connection with any Client, Case, or otherwise. (…)”&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 05 November 2025 16:49To: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;Hi all&nbsp;I've just been speaking to Helena about the below. She suggested that @Carolina Koschdoski de Souza&nbsp;might be able to assist quicker with the information required for this witness statement. This witness statement must be served by 4pm Friday 7th&nbsp;(this week) so we really need this info tonight/tomorrow. See the yellow highlights specifically. Also (appreciating you are juggling an enormous workload) if the A&amp;R execution has to slip so we can finalise this statement I would much rather that as this is court ordered and we can explain the timing.&nbsp;@Carolina Koschdoski de Souza&nbsp;give me a call if you want to discuss.&nbsp;ThanksAnna&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, November 5, 2025 3:04 PMTo:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;FW: Disclosure application - AA2 WS &nbsp;Hi all&nbsp;Following up on the email from Pallas yesterday asking for input on the funding disclosure statement, would it be possible to get your input on these points this afternoon? &nbsp;I attach the latest draft of the statement for reference.&nbsp;In case helpful to get the ball rolling I have tried to allocate the relevant points below but please do let me know if there is someone else better placed to answer.&nbsp;Also just a minor formatting point, but just to note that the paragraph numbering seems to have gone awry in that it restarts from 23 in Section IV so some of the paragraph references are confusing. I will flag this to Pallas on response.&nbsp;ThanksJess&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom:&nbsp;Amy Hobbs &lt;Amy.Hobbs@pallasllp.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;04 November 2025 13:43To:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Erika Saluzzo &lt;esaluzzo@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;All,&nbsp;By way of brief introduction for those I have not met yet - &nbsp;I have recently joined Pallas as an Associate and I am assisting the team on this matter.&nbsp;Please see as follows a list of our queries for you in the witness statement in case it is helpful to have in one place. Paragraph references below relate to the draft witness statement circulated by Matt at 11:49 on 4/11/25 (attached). &nbsp;PG to please:1)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Confirm:1.&nbsp; who/what is referred to in the Legal Futures article dated 2 October 2023 (see para 25) @Alicia Alinia “In a Legal Futures article from 2 October 2023 (paragraph 21(b)), I am quoted as saying that certain funding “was allocated to specific cases”.&nbsp; Mr Boddy states that this was a description of Gramercy funding arrangements. That is incorrect: this statement referred to other funders.” See full article attached (NOX1D12_2) in case helpful @Carolina Koschdoski de Souza&nbsp;do you know what this is - see the attachment.b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; accuracy of the proposed wording at paras 28.1 and 29 &nbsp;(and any comments on accuracy of the witness statement more generally) @Helena Yearwood, @Alicia Alinia28.1 The PG Claimants’ estimated figures [in the Second General Budget and the Tranche 3 Budget] have been adopted for phases which do not yet have court approved sums (the Expert Report Phase of the Tranche 3 Budget and the ADR Phase of the Second General Budget). Please confirm the highlighted wording is accurate.&nbsp;29&nbsp;“At paragraph 83, Mr Boddy speculates that there is an arrangement between Pogust Goodhead, Gramercy and these funders. There is no such arrangement” Please confirm this is accurate @Carolina Koschdoski de Souzac)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; the dates of PG’s responses to non-lead GLOs letters received on 20 and 21 October 2025 (see para 27) – I am looking into thisd)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; whether PG has disclosed financial statements/ Fulcrum and Locke funding documents (see para 28) @Helena Yearwood, @Alicia Aliniae)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;status of the funding with Fulcrum and Locke (see para 28) @Helena Yearwoodf)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; what the loans in WJB/538-540 are and whether any of them are prior Gramercy funding (see para 31) – See extract of relevant pages attached. @Tom Crow are you able to confirm?g)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; whether we ever informed the Defendants of when the Gramercy funding started in correspondence (see para 31) @Helena Yearwood are you aware of this? I can also have a look through previous correspondence.2)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Populate Opus references as required throughout / let Pallas know which documents are not on Opus for Pallas to exhibit – I will deal with this.3)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Provide Pallas with the following documents:a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; a copy of NOX1D12/5 I’ll share thisb)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; a copy of the letter Anna mentioned following her review of the statement (see para 26) regarding the allegation that PG have set unreasonably tight deadlines in correspondence throughout the trial phase. I will find thisc)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;timestamp of the emails attaching (i) McGuire Woods letter dated 1 October 2025 (see para 26.2) Timestamp 20:05 ; and (ii) Quinn letter dated 22 October 2023 (see para 26.4) I’m looking into this4)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Keep Pallas updated with progress of discussions to secure further ATE cover @Helena Yearwood&nbsp;– maybe we could provide Pallas with a status update at the end of the day today?&nbsp;Many thanks,Amy&nbsp;Amy&nbsp;Hobbs​​​​AssociateT: +44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1056|M: +44&nbsp;7751&nbsp;928&nbsp;570E:&nbsp; amy.hobbs@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom:&nbsp;Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;04 November 2025 11:49To:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; b.williams@4newsquare.comCc:&nbsp;Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Erika Saluzzo &lt;esaluzzo@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Disclosure application - AA2 WS&nbsp;Theo, Ben and PG team&nbsp;Please see attached a new version of the witness statement, along with a redline against the version Anna sent back to us yesterday morning.&nbsp;There remain a number of questions for PG – we will send you a separate list"}

