ails about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt; Sent: 08 December 2025 16:36To: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: M Burke&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Natasha,&nbsp;I hope you had a nice weekend.&nbsp;Further to the below, can you let me know when you will be in a position to respond?&nbsp;&nbsp;As previously advised, the loss of two weeks full pay is not trivial. If it is the company's position that it has appropriately and clearly advised me of a change to what you have termed the contractual framework, then I will need to consider going against the clear medical advice I have been provided and returning to work sooner than I have been advised.&nbsp;&nbsp;On the company's current stance, I am already at a loss of 6 days full pay and the longer this situation exists, the more at a detriment I will be.&nbsp;If you can let me know as soon as possible that would be appreciated.&nbsp;Kind regards,Michael&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Sent: Friday, December 5, 2025 6:16:41 PMTo: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: M Burke &nbsp;Hi Natasha,&nbsp;Thank you for responding, and on your non-working day.&nbsp;&nbsp;I am sure as you will appreciate I am keep to resolve this as quickly as possible, especially in light of it becoming new information to me that the company is stating I am not eligible for OSP when I was anticipating that I would be. Two weeks full pay is not a trivial sum of money.&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Friday, December 5, 2025 6:04:01 PMTo: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt