e on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt; Sent: 04 December 2025 21:07To: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; HR Team &lt;hr@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: M Burke&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Dear Colleagues,&nbsp;Having received an out of office from Natasha advising she is out of office until Monday 8 December, and given the urgency to establish the position regarding the Sickness Policy and SSP, I am forwarding this email to the HR inbox.&nbsp;I look forward to hearing from you.&nbsp;Kind regards,Michael&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Thursday, December 4, 2025 9:00 pmTo:&nbsp;Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: M Burke &nbsp;Dear Natasha,&nbsp;Thank you for your email and for providing responses to my queries.&nbsp;&nbsp;Firstly, thank you for confirming that my final pay will include payment for my six days accrued but untaken annual in addition to the pro-rated acting up allowance for the 15 days of employment with the firm in December.&nbsp;Thank you also for confirming the position of the company equipment, it is relieving to hear that as long as the courier collects this on the 12th, there will not be any withheld payment if they do not deliver it by the 15th. Please let me know the details of the courier so I can ensure the equipment is not in use and is ready to be collected.&nbsp;I will attend the office to return the remainder of my equipment (noting some of it remains in the flat in London along with some of my personal items so I need to be in London to deal with that in any event).&nbsp;&nbsp;With regard to the OSP v SSP, thank you for confirming the point regarding the Sickness Policy.&nbsp;&nbsp;I am afraid I do not think I have ever been provided with this. Can you please provide me with this?&nbsp;I also not the firm's position that the policy has been applied consistently. I reserve my position on this for now.&nbsp;Additionally, should I need to return to work, contrary to specific medical advice I.e. the medical document I have provided confirming that I should not be working, on account of being required to, to be eligible for full pay, then I also reserve my position on this.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thank you again for turning this around and for the confirmations provided.&nbsp;&nbsp;I look forward to hearing from you.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom:&nbsp;Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Thursday, December 4, 2025 8:20:27 PMT"}

